ef","ingredient/beef"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Corn husks","ingredient/corn-husks"],["Cornmeal","ingredient/cornmeal"],["Maize","ingredient/maize"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]},{"h":"Mentioned in","links":[["Nahua foodways","cuisine/nahua-foodways"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/3/3b/Masa_de_tortillas.jpg/500px-Masa_de_tortillas.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Artemisa Martínez","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masa_de_tortillas.jpg"}},"dish/wei-wurst":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/wei-wurst","n":"Weißwurst","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Weißwurst is a traditional Bavarian sausage made from minced veal and pork fatback. It is usually flavored with parsley, lemon, mace, onions, ginger and cardamom, although there are some variations. The mixture is stuffed into pork casings and separated into individual sausages measuring about 10 to 12 cm (3+7⁄8–4+3⁄4 in) in length and 3–4 cm (1+1⁄8–1+5⁄8 in) in diameter. In Poland, a similar kind of sausage, also named 'white sausage' (biała kiełbasa), is made from pork instead and most often served on Easter."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-wei-wurst"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wei%C3%9Fwurst"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Bavarian cuisine","cuisine/bavarian-cuisine"],["Hamburg cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-hamburg"],["Silesian cuisine","cuisine/silesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"]]},{"h":"More from Bavarian cuisine","links":[["Bayrisch Kraut","dish/bayrisch-kraut"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Rumford's Soup","dish/rumford-s-soup"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/2/21/Weisswurst_of_Bavaria_with_Prezels.jpg/500px-Weisswurst_of_Bavaria_with_Prezels.jpg","w":500,"h":254,"by":"Burkhard Mücke","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Weisswurst_of_Bavaria_with_Prezels.jpg"}}}